<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="09">
<name>SRS Airbag &amp; Seat Belt</name>
<section id="1002M_S001G" variety="S001G">
<name>Pre-crash Safety</name>
<ttl id="1002M_S001G_74WT7_T00FP" variety="T00FP">
<name>Pre-crash Safety System</name>
<para id="RM000002NJ6004X" category="C" type-id="8004P" name-id="540JQ-00" from="200708">
<dtccode>U0122/51</dtccode>
<dtcname>VSC → Distance Control ECU Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>U0100/51</dtccode>
<dtcname>Engine ECU Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>U1101/51</dtccode>
<dtcname>Distance Control ECU Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002NJ6004X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CTH00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The seat belt control computer communicates information with each ECU via CAN communication. A DTC is output when communication with an ECU cannot be established.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0122/51</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Lost communication or communication failure from the ABS &amp; traction actuator assembly to the seat belt control computer</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>CAN Communication System</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0100/51</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Lost communication or communication failure from the engine control computer to the distance control computer assembly</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>CAN Communication System</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U1101/51</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Lost communication or communication failure from the distance control computer assembly to the seat belt control computer</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>CAN Communication System</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002NJ6004X_02" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002NJ6004X_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000002NJ6004X_03_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CTI00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Read DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON and record the DTCs following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000006EM00JX"/>)</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If CAN communication system DTCs and DTCs other than CAN communication system DTCs are output at the same time, troubleshoot the non-CAN communication DTCs after the CAN communication malfunction has returned to normal.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002NJ6004X_03_0002" fin="true">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002NJ6004X_03_0002">
<testtitle>Go to CAN Communication System<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001R4W00DX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
